sequenceDiagram
    participant U as U: gets/read
    participant T as trampoline
    participant S as S: syscall/read
    participant C as UART/PLIC
    participant B as ring[128]
    U->>T: ecall, a7=read
    T->>S: save trapframe, switch to kernel stack
    S->>B: inspect input_count
    alt empty
        S->>S: enable interrupt and wait
        C->>T: external interrupt
        T->>S: consoleintr
        S->>B: append byte, count newline
    else available
        S->>B: consume through newline
    end
    B-->>S: n bytes
    S->>T: a0=n, restore registers
    T-->>U: sret to next user instruction
    Note over B: Analysis: full ring drops the oldest byte on overflow;
    Note over U,S: Analysis: newline bounds one read even in character-stream mode.
